e=\"white-space: normal; width: auto; left: 0;\"><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></pre></div>","timeToRead":1,"excerpt":"A neat way of always cleaning up resources is to use Lambdas as data. Take the following. Source Usage We are now guaranteed that in the case of an exception the resources will get cleaned up. Usage…","frontmatter":{"title":"Resource Cleanup and Lambda Expressions","date":"03 November 2009","category":".NET & C#","tags":["lambdas","design patterns"],"image":null}}},"pageContext":{"slug":"/blog/2009-11-03-resource-cleanup-and-lambda-expressions/"}},"staticQueryHashes":["764694655"],"slicesMap":{}}